        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: King of Norway, King Magnus, Norwegian king\n- Places: Southern Isles, island, Norse world\n- Topics: military campaigns, naming, Norse names\n\nFacts:\n- The Southern Isles was a Norse name for an island group that was at times independent of external control.\n- A King of Norway launched aggressive military campaigns in the Southern Isles.\n- King Magnus' Halt railway station was named after King Magnus.\n- The king associated with King Magnus' Halt railway station was the same King of Norway who campaigned in the Southern Isles.",
